### Env / secrets ###
# Root-level .env holds real Docker Compose secrets (JWT_SECRET, POSTGRES_PASSWORD,
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID) - see .env.example for the template. Nested .env files (e.g.
# frontend/.env) are placeholder-only templates and are meant to be committed.
/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.development.local
**/.env.test.local
**/.env.production.local

